# Profile: daily-driver coding model — scale-out (one independent instance per Spark).
# Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B: coding-tuned MoE (~3B active), prefix caching works, ~30-48 tok/s.
# FP8 is high-quality + safe on the eugr image; swap to an AWQ build if you prefer.
PROFILE_NAME=local-coder
PROFILE_MODE=scaleout                  # run on both nodes; gateway load-balances

VLLM_IMAGE=vllm-node
VLLM_MODEL=Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct-FP8
VLLM_SERVED_NAME=local-coder           # gateway routes "local-coder" here
VLLM_MAX_LEN=131072
# NOTE: 128GB is UNIFIED CPU+GPU memory. At startup, page cache (e.g. from a just-downloaded
# model) can transiently lower the driver's "free memory" reading, and vLLM sizes its pool against
# TOTAL device mem — so a high util can fail the startup free-memory check. 0.60 of 119GB = ~72GB
# is plenty for a 30B model + KV and leaves margin. (The GNOME desktop is masked/headless on both
# nodes, but that frees ~0 RAM on these boxes — the limiter is model size + KV, not the GUI.)
VLLM_GPU_UTIL=0.60
VLLM_MAX_SEQS=8                         # lots of headroom on this model
VLLM_ARGS=                              # extra vllm serve args, if any
